ight the words that we deliberately  learn and study on flash cards that's a  small part of the words that we are at  least can learn should learn in fact if  we spend too much time deliberately  trying to master a few words we will end  up knowing fewer words  and so i liken it a bit too i don't know  if you play scrabble but the people who  play scrabble by trying to make very  little clever little words it if you  know where they get nine points ten  points and use two letters they lose the  idea in scrabble is to use up as many  letters as possible so that your  opponent doesn't get as many letters to  play with it's a volume thing and it's  the same in language learning the more  words you know the more words you can  guess at because  very often the new word that you come  across say at our  lesson pages link which is therefore  still blue  it might be a form of a word that you  already know or something that contains  components of words that you already  know so you don't need to save that word  because you can basically guess what the  meaning is and if you guess wrong or if  you have any doubt you can always look  it up again but i tend not to you know i  look at this word i say yeah i kind of  know what it means in this context fine  i'll take it and i don't even worry  about whether i know all of the possible  you know the full range or scope of that  word i know enough of this word to get  me through this content that i'm reading  and listening to because ultimately it's  this massive exposure to interesting  content content that is interesting to  me and yet that i can make sense of  within this context  that's what's going to make me improve  in the language that's going to give me  more and more exposure and so you want  to move as quickly as possible to where  you can kind of work through interesting  content you understand these words you  can guess at new words and pretty soon  all of a sudden texts that seemed  difficult three months ago are now  easier for you you are acquiring these  words incidentally  now  as i've said many many times for that to  work you have to move very quickly  through relatively uninteresting content  in order to get or you can focus on  things of interest to you which might be  history music literature whatever it is  that you're interested in in my own case  i'm very interested in history so i  spent a lot of time recently  reading interesting articles books  listening to stuff related to ukrainian  history and there's no question that i'm  improving i just finished having a very  good conversation with uh katerina in  dinipro and in fact i  i did a video with her some while ago  where and this would showed my level in  ukrainian and i'm going to ask her  perhaps the next time or whenever uh  that to ask her if she would do another  video with  us having a conversation in ukrainian  and you'll see how much my ukrainian has  improved my vocabulary my comprehension  my ability to use words not only which  words belong together but even getting  the grammar right the instrumental the  dative whatever all of this stuff is  falling into place because i'm just  consuming more and more words so uh you  know i liken it to a snowball you know  language learning is a volume thing it's  a big data kind of thing it's not  picking away at little knits nuts and  bolts trying to nail down this or that  making sure i  master this word i know it you know it's  got to be become part of my active  vocabulary stuff forget all that stuff  know enough of the word to get through  interesting content and then expose  yourself to as much as possible of stuff  that interests you compelling content  and then when you feel up to it start  using it and when you use it of course  you'll see where you're missing things  you're you're not totally confident  about this word or that where you use it  right or you use it wrong and then you  go back and listen some more and you're  just gathering like a snowball you're  just gathering and gathering more words  in language learning it's a bit like you  know the rich get richer and the poor  get poorer the more money you have the  more money you can make because you can  invest it and you can earn more and more  money because you have money on the  other hand  uh you know if you the same with words  so the more words you hold there was  just something flashed on my screen here  the more words you have the more words  you can learn the more of the jigsaw  puzzle of the language becomes clear the  more  fuzzy and unclear things you can now  start to focus on and make them clear  okay so yeah  after some of the uh  is also for putting them so there's some  practice  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  that's all for today see you  next time thank you for listening  [Music]  you

